.TH PCLOUD-ARCHIVE 1 "2026-08-26" "pcloud-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pcloud-archive \- copy a configured local folder directly to pcloud-crypt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcloud-archive
.RB [ \-\-config " " CONFIG ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pcloud-archive
performs a manual, one-way copy from a configured local source folder to a
.B pcloud-crypt:
remote using rclone.
The crypt mount is not required.
Missing or changed files are copied, while files deleted locally are not
automatically deleted from pCloud.
.PP
This command is not a bidirectional sync tool and does not implement
.BR "rsync --delete" .
.SH FIRST-TIME SETUP
Create
.I ~/.config/pcloud-archive/config.toml
and configure an existing local
.B source_root
plus the destination
.BR remote_root .
.PP
Use
.B pcloud-archive help config
to see the keys and a complete example, or create a non-overwriting
starter file with:
.PP
.EX
pcloud-archive help config --init-config ~/.config/pcloud-archive/config.toml
.EE
.PP
.EX
[defaults]
profile = "mac"

[profiles.mac]
source_root = "/absolute/path/to/local/archive-source"
remote_root = "pcloud-crypt:archive"
.EE
.PP
Do not use
.I ~/p-crypt
or
.I ~/.pcloud/crypt
as
.BR source_root ;
those are mounted views of the destination.
.SH TYPICAL WORKFLOW
.EX
pcloud-archive doctor
pcloud-archive diff
pcloud-archive promote . --dry-run
pcloud-archive promote . --execute
pcloud-archive check . --execute
.EE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Show command help. Use
.B help --detail
to rediscover the manual page and the full Markdown documentation.
Use
.B help config
for the configuration schema and
.B help config --init-config <config-path>
to create a starter file without overwriting an existing file.
.TP
.B info
Show resolved configuration, runtime state, paths, and impact scope.
Use
.B info paths
to rediscover files and documentation.
.TP
.B doctor
Check configuration, the local source, rclone, and pcloud-crypt connectivity.
The crypt mount and this manual page are not runtime requirements.
.TP
.B status
Show manifest counts, tombstones, and the latest recorded run.
.TP
.B diff
Compare the configured local source with the remote without copying files.
.TP
.B promote
Preview or execute a one-way
.B rclone copy
for a path under
.BR source_root .
.TP
.B check
Run
.B rclone check --one-way
and record a successful verification.
.TP
.B delete-canonical
Preview or explicitly delete one remote file and record a tombstone.
.TP
.B drop-cache
Preview local cleanup without deleting anything from pCloud.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is resolved in this order: command-line flags,
environment variables,
.I ~/.config/pcloud-archive/config.toml,
then safe built-in defaults.
rclone owns pCloud credentials; no pCloud secret is required in this
config file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pcloud-archive/config.toml
Persistent configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pcloud-archive/<profile>/manifest.json
Successful verification records.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pcloud-archive/<profile>/tombstones.json
Remote deletion tombstones.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pcloud-archive/<profile>/last-run.json
Latest recorded mutating or verification run.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
The complete documentation is stored under:
.PP
.I /Users/takafumi/p-core/dev/#仕様書/pcloud-archive/
.PP
Use these commands to rediscover the current paths:
.PP
.EX
pcloud-archive help --detail
pcloud-archive info paths
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when a command succeeds or when diagnostics contain only
nonblocking information.
Returns nonzero for invalid or missing required configuration,
inaccessible sources, unavailable required commands or remotes,
and failed operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
